==Description==

La commande [[Image:CfdOF_MeshFromShape.svg|24px]] '''CfdOF Maillage à partir d'une forme''' crée un objet contenant les données nécessaires à la génération d'un maillage à partir d'une géométrie. Ces données peuvent être modifiées dans un panneau de tâches.

<span id="Usage"></span>
==Utilisation==

<span id="Create_mesh_data_object"></span>
===Créer un objet de données d'un maillage===

# Si nécessaire : activez le [[Image:CfdOF_Analysis.svg|16px]] [[CfdOF_Analysis/fr|conteneur d'analyse]] approprié en double-cliquant dessus dans l'[[Tree_View/fr|arborescence]].
# Sélectionnez la géométrie à mailler.
# Il existe plusieurs façons de lancer la commande :
#* Cliquez sur le bouton {{Button|[[Image:CfdOF_MeshFromShape.svg|16px]] [[CfdOF_MeshFromShape/fr|CFD mesh]]}}.
#* Sélectionnez l'option {{MenuCommand|CfdOF → [[Image:CfdOF_MeshFromShape.svg|16px]] CFD mesh}} du menu.
# Un objet de données [[Image:CfdOF_MeshFromShape.svg|16px]] '''[GeometryName]_Mesh''' est ajouté au conteneur.
# Le panneau des tâches s'ouvre. Voir [[#Options|Options]] pour plus d'informations.
# Cliquez sur le bouton {{Button|Fermer}} pour terminer la commande.

<span id="Edit_mesh_data_object"></span>
===Modifier un objet de données d'un maillage===

# Procédez de l'une des manières suivantes :
#* Suivez les étapes 1 et 3 décrites ci-dessus.
#* Double-cliquez sur un objet de données [[Image:CfdOF_MeshFromShape.svg|16px]] '''[GeometryName]_Mesh''' dans l'arborescence.
# Le panneau de tâches s'ouvre. Voir [[#Options|Options]] pour plus d'informations.
# Appuyez sur le bouton {{Button|Fermer}} pour terminer la commande.

==Options==

Le panneau des tâches propose les paramètres suivants : 

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
[[File:CfdOF_DialogCFDMesh2.png|393px|frameless|center|alt=CfdOF CFD Mesh task panel|CfdOF CFD Mesh task panel]]
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
===Mesh Parameters===
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
'''Mesh Utility''' dropdown box gives the following options:
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
*'''cfMesh'''
: [https://cfmesh.com/cfmesh-open-source/ cfMesh] is an open-source, extensible library for automatic mesh generation. cfMesh supports both 3D and 2D meshes and can generate:
:* Hex dominant 3D meshes
:* Quad dominant 2D meshes
:* Tetrahedral dominant 3D meshes
:* Polyhedral dominant 3D meshes
 
*'''gmsh (tetrahedral)'''
*'''gmsh (polyhedral)'''
: [https://gmsh.info/ Gmsh] is an open source 3D finite element mesh generator.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
*'''snappyHexMesh'''
: [https://doc.cfd.direct/openfoam/user-guide-v11/snappyhexmesh snappyHexMesh] is an automatic split hex mesher which refines and snaps to surface. It generates 3D meshes containing hexahedra and split-hexahedra from a triangulated surface geometry in Stereolithography (STL) format. snappyHexMesh is used for complex geometries.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
'''Base element size''' input box
: The Base, or Background, Mesh is the initial mesh, without refinement. If left as 0, it will default to 2 % of bounding box characteristic length. e.g. a 10 mm square cube will have boundary box characteristics of (10<sup>2</sup> + 10<sup>2</sup> + 10<sup>2</sup>)<sup>0.5</sup> of which 2% is 0.35mm.
</div>  

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
===snappyHexMesh parameters===
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
The following parameters are only available when the snappyHexMesh Mesh Utility has been selected.
</div>  

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
[[File:CfdOF_DialogCFDMesh.png|393px|frameless|center|alt=CfdOF CFD Mesh task panel snappyHexMesh|CfdOF CFD Mesh task panel snappyHexMesh]]
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
'''Point in mesh'''
: Enter a location vector inside the region to be meshed, in the form x, y,	z. This is used to identify whether the geometry is to be meshed on the outside, as in the case of fluid flowing over a pipe, or the inside, as in fluid flowing through a pipe. The {{Button|'''Search'''}} button will try to locate a position in the region to be meshed.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
'''No. of cells between levels''' & '''Relative edge refinement'''
: The '''base element size''' has already been defined above. Volume or surface refinement is achieved by splitting the base cells into 4 quads for 2D or 8 hexes for 3D models. The figure below shows the base cell being split into 4 quads at the first split n=1 and then each new cell being again split into 4 quads on the second spit, n=2.
</div> 

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
[[File:CfdOF-MeshCellSplit.png|544px|frameless|center|alt=CfdOF CFD Mesh Cell Split|CfdOF Mesh Cell Split]]
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
: The '''Relative edge refinement''' input box accepts values between 0.001 and 1. It defines the mesh size relative to the starting background mesh. The split can be calculated by 1/(2^n-1) e.g. for n=2, the relative edge refinement value is 0.5.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
: To achieve a smooth transition between the split cells, ensure that there are a number of cells between consecutive refinement levels. The '''No. of cells between levels''' input box accepts integer values above or equal to 1 with a default value of 3.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
[[File:CfdOF MeshCellSplitn2.png|100px|frameless|center|alt=Mesh Cell Split with refinement level 2|Mesh Cell Split with refinement level 2]]
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
: The above example has a refinement level of n=2 giving a relative edge refinement of 0.5 with 2 cells between consecutive refinement levels.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
'''Edge detection''' 
*'''Implicit''' snaps to automatically detected surface geometric feature edges.
*'''Explicit''' snaps to manually generated feature edges.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
===Meshing===
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
{{Button|'''Write mesh case'''}} button 
: Clicking on the '''Write mesh case''' creates the mesh files with the progress being displayed in the '''Status''' box.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
{{Button|'''Edit'''}} button
: The '''Edit''' button opens the directory where the OpenFOAM case files are stored, including the mesh files, generated above, in the constant directory. For more information about these files and directories please visit the UNDER THE HOOD PAGE.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
{{Button|'''Run mesher'''}} button
: Clicking on the '''Run mesher''' button starts the selected mesher process, with the progress being displayed in the '''Status''' box.
</div> 

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
{{Button|'''Stop'''}} button
: Used to stop either the '''Write mesh case''' or '''Run mesher''' processes.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
===Visualisation===
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
{{Button|'''Paraview'''}} button
: ParaView is an open-source, multi-platform data analysis and visualization application. Clicking on the '''Paraview''' button opens the mesher, to allow the mesh to be inspected.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
{{Button|'''Check Mesh'''}} button
: Clicking on the '''Check Mesh''' button runs the OpenFOAM checkMesh utility. This checks the validity of a mesh and outputs it’s result in the reports view area in FreeCAD. It’s possible to enlarge this box, by dragging the top of the reports panel up the screen.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
{{Button|'''Load surface mesh'''}} button
: Clicking on '''Load surface mesh''' displays the mesh on the geometry within FreeCad. It only the displays the mesh on the surface of the geometry and not the internals. For a more detailed inspection of the mesh use ParaView. 
: Warning! If the message in the '''Status''' reads: 
:: "Triangulated representation of the surface mesh is shown - Please use Paraview for full mesh visualisation." 
: The '''Load surface mesh''' image displayed is not fully representative of the mesh and you should view the mesh in ParaView.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
{{Button|'''Clear'''}} button
: The '''Clear''' button removes the mesh on the geometry within FreeCad.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
'''Status''' output box
: When clicking {{Button|'''Write mesh case'''}} or {{Button|'''Run mesher'''}}, the progress is displayed in the '''Status''' output box, together with any error messages. 
:* When {{Button|'''Write mesh case'''}} has finished, the last message in the '''Status''' output box will be 'Mesh case written successfully'.
:* When {{Button|'''Run mesher'''}} has finished, the last message in the '''Status''' output box will be 'Meshing completed'.
</div>

